¬import il from "../../../../../../_shared/variables/imageLinks"


2.  Locate the **`"language"`** property. *- red rectangle*

    - This property tells CSpell which spoken language locale to use when selecting its general dictionary.

3. Change its value to the language code for the language you want the dictionary to use. *- yellow rectangle*
    - To use **Canadian English** for example, set the value to `"en-CA"`.

    ```json
    "language": "en-CA",
    ```

    > You can also enable multiple languages by separating the codes with a comma, for example: `"language": "en,fr"`.


